1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,270
This is ORYN.

2
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:05,300
Pay links that split themselves, on Celo.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,630
Getting paid is one moment. What comes after is a chore.

4
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:16,210
You pay your designer their cut, move some into savings, and keep the rest. By hand, every single time.

5
00:00:16,380 --> 00:00:22,630
And if your client is new to crypto, asking them to buy CELO just for gas is usually where the deal stalls.

6
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:25,860
ORYN turns all of that into a link.

7
00:00:26,030 --> 00:00:31,270
Set your rules once, share a link, and your client signs once, with no gas.

8
00:00:31,440 --> 00:00:36,970
ORYN's agent splits the money onchain within seconds. It's live on Celo mainnet today.

9
00:00:37,660 --> 00:00:43,520
Start at oryn.click/vault and connect MiniPay, Valora or MetaMask.

10
00:00:43,690 --> 00:00:50,800
Add who gets what. Here, 60% goes to a collaborator and 10% to savings. The rest stays yours.

11
00:00:50,970 --> 00:00:55,780
One transaction creates your own vault contract. It's yours, not ours.

12
00:00:56,480 --> 00:01:02,320
This is your vault: balances, your split, pay links, activity and withdrawals.

13
00:01:02,490 --> 00:01:07,800
It's all read straight from the chain. There's no database. Your rules live in your contract.

14
00:01:08,500 --> 00:01:11,270
Creating a pay link takes one sentence.

15
00:01:11,440 --> 00:01:20,090
Type "charge 25 USAT for the logo design, monthly" and ORYN fills in the form. It works in Spanish and Portuguese too.

16
00:01:20,260 --> 00:01:24,660
Then copy the link, show a QR code, or send it straight to WhatsApp.

17
00:01:24,830 --> 00:01:30,760
Paying a subcontractor? Switch on private split, and your client sees the amount, not who gets what.

18
00:01:31,450 --> 00:01:36,930
Here's what your client sees: the amount, what it's for, and exactly how it will be split.

19
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:40,010
In English, Spanish or Portuguese.

20
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:45,970
Before anything moves, ORYN screens the payer against Chainalysis' onchain sanctions list.

21
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:56,270
Then your client pays in USA₮ with a single signature. No gas, no CELO. Celo's x402 facilitator settles it straight into your vault.

22
00:01:56,970 --> 00:01:59,160
This is a real payment on mainnet.

23
00:01:59,330 --> 00:02:05,260
An independent wallet, active on Celo since 2021, paid 1 USA₮.

24
00:02:05,430 --> 00:02:12,250
Seconds later, ORYN's agent split it: 90% to the collaborator, 10% kept as savings.

25
00:02:12,420 --> 00:02:18,190
Every payment gets a receipt like this, read from the chain, that anyone can print and check.

26
00:02:18,890 --> 00:02:20,910
And everything is public.

27
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:27,520
The proof page lists every payment into every ORYN vault, how it settled, and the split that followed.

28
00:02:27,690 --> 00:02:35,040
For each payer it checks when the wallet first used Celo and who funded it, so you can see which payments are truly independent.

29
00:02:35,210 --> 00:02:37,880
Our own tests are labelled, never hidden.

30
00:02:38,580 --> 00:02:41,320
ORYN is built for AI agents too.

31
00:02:41,490 --> 00:02:46,560
Every pay link is a standard x402 resource that any agent can pay.

32
00:02:46,730 --> 00:02:56,910
With the ORYN MCP server, Claude, Cursor or any agent can read a vault, check a link's split, create pay links and pay them, capped at the amount you allow.

33
00:02:57,610 --> 00:02:59,630
Your money is never ours.

34
00:02:59,800 --> 00:03:07,870
The agent can run your split. It can never withdraw, and it can never change your rules. That's enforced in the vault contract, not promised.

35
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:13,730
Every transaction carries our attribution tag, and the agent has its own onchain ERC-8004 identity.

36
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:17,810
ORYN. Get paid in dollars, split on arrival.

37
00:03:17,980 --> 00:03:20,000
Try it at oryn.click

